# set test time
# Year is pinned explicitly (not left at TIME's own wall-clock default)
# so south-west-shade's own SHADE_DATE_ANGLE - driven by a real date -
# can't drift from one baseline regeneration to the next just because
# of which real year happens to be current when this runs: for a
# January date, dateAngleFromRealDate's own terminalYear
# reduces to this same year, and its leap-status alone shifts the angle
# by about a degree (294 in a leap year vs 295 in a common one) - small,
# but enough to invalidate the committed baseline for no reason related
# to this app's own behavior. 2025 is a common year, matching the angle
# (295 degrees) the current committed baseline was generated under.
Year 2025
Month 1
Day 15

# clear default model
Delete all

3d-model 3

Delete All Model2Ds

Person m=1 x=-20 y=0   z=0
Person m=2 x=20  y=0   z=0
Person m=3 x=0   y=-20 z=0
Person m=4 x=0   y=20  z=0

